{"availability":"available","full":"mastodon/mastodon","name":"mastodon","description":"Your self-hosted, globally interconnected microblogging community","category":"Productivity","language":"Ruby","stars":50344,"forks":7504,"created":"2016-02-22T15:01:25Z","updated":"2026-10-04T05:59:02Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://joinmastodon.org","topics":["activity-stream","activitypub","docker","fediverse","mastodon","microblog","social-network","social-web","webfinger"],"demo":null,"color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T06:11:03.733Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T06:11:03.733Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T06:11:03.733Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T06:11:03.733Z","discoveredVia":[{"kind":"curated-list","name":"Awesome Selfhosted","url":"https://github.com/awesome-selfhosted/awesome-selfhosted"}],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T06:11:03.733Z","stars":50344,"forks":7504}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Want to learn more about Mastodon? Click below to find out more in a video.","Mastodon is a free, open-source social network server based on ActivityPub where users can follow friends and discover new ones. On Mastodon, users can publish anything they want: links, pictures, text, and video. All Mastodon servers are interoperable as a federated network (users on one server can seamlessly communicate with users from another one, including non-Mastodon software that implements ActivityPub!)"],"features":["Part of the Fediverse. Based on open standards, with no vendor lock-in. - the network goes beyond just Mastodon; anything that implements ActivityPub is part of a broader social network known as the Fediverse. You can…","Real-time, chronological timeline updates - updates of people you're following appear in real-time in the UI.","Media attachments - upload and view images and videos attached to the updates. Videos with no audio track are treated like animated GIFs; normal videos loop continuously.","Safety and moderation tools - Mastodon includes private posts, locked accounts, phrase filtering, muting, blocking, and many other features, along with a reporting and moderation system.","OAuth2 and a straightforward REST API - Mastodon acts as an OAuth2 provider, and third party apps can use the REST and Streaming APIs. This results in a rich app ecosystem with a variety of choices!"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mastodon/mastodon/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"fc19a5dcbef5fb5b018055e5bda0426087dc576384305ed130704dac8f81d144","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T05:14:13.358Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T06:11:03.733Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Want to learn more about Mastodon? Click below to find out more in a video.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mastodon/mastodon/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"fc19a5dcbef5fb5b018055e5bda0426087dc576384305ed130704dac8f81d144","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mastodon/mastodon/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T06:11:03.733Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-04T05:59:02Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mastodon/mastodon/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T06:11:03.733Z","hash":"fc19a5dcbef5fb5b018055e5bda0426087dc576384305ed130704dac8f81d144","originalBytes":5843,"storedBytes":5843,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["mastodon","license","other","software","users","affero","development","free","general","gnu","network","public","activitypub","follow","like","project","rest","should","under","videos","about","along","any","anything","api","based","browserstack","chromatic","contributing","copyright","deployment","documentation.","eugen","features","guide","help","implements","includes","including","learn","licensed","main","moderation","node.js","oauth2","one","open-source","part","postgresql","powers","program","read","real-time","redis","repository","rochko","ruby","see","serve